From b5ffd845251b330d95f2e30b35aecb20fd0d5cd5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paul Hogan
 <5004d00b753726762516a66df75936687319095eacf0e9f7a4710f7a0ff12098@meshllm.communities.buzz.xyz>
Date: Fri, 28 Aug 2026 22:26:14 +1000
Subject: [PATCH] skippy: admit shared-KV reuse anchors into stage memory and
 seed them cross-stage

Gemma3N and Gemma4 alias the KV cache of every layer above
n_layer_kv_from_start to one of two anchor layers (n-2 for SWA, n-1 for
full attention); those reuse layers compute no K/V of their own. A stage
slice starting above the anchors filtered them out of stage memory, so
the reuse lookup asserted (SIGABRT) at model open - Gemma-4 E4B aborted
at every split >= 23.

- skippy_stage_memory_filter now admits the two reuse anchors into stage
  memory (allocation only; the stage graph filter still excludes them)
- the kv-cache reuse assert becomes a thrown runtime error, surfaced as
  a clean stage-open failure instead of a process abort
- stage_seed_kv_page writes anchor rows into a fresh cache without
  marking cells or advancing position: the next decode claims the same
  cells and reads the seeded rows in place (a plain import would
  double-allocate the position and leave a zero row visible)
- skippy_session_shared_kv_anchor_range +
  skippy_session_seed_shared_kv_anchor_page expose the transport;
  composite ISWA export tolerates zero-layer base/SWA components when
  the anchor range selects only one of the two subcaches

ABI patch 42 -> 43. Validated: Gemma-4 E4B Q4_K_M Metal 36/36 cuts 6..41
exact parity (deep cuts 23..41 previously aborted); Qwen3.5-4B 31/31
unchanged.
